cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these skills or the conversion method, please cite the originating Cognition Today work."
title: "Simulated Cognitive Skills for LLM Creativity and Metacognition"
abstract: >-
  Agent Skills that convert cognitive-psychology frameworks published on Cognition
  Today into explicit, auditable agent procedures with bounded activation, source
  provenance, state contracts, and documented failure conditions. The skills
  simulate the structure of human cognitive functions as executable procedures;
  they do not claim the functions themselves. This release contains two domain
  skills, Simulated Metacognition (monitor-and-regulate-thinking) and Simulated
  Creative Cognition (create-through-recomposition), and the shared runtime they
  coordinate with, Simulated Working Memory (manage-working-context), which
  preserves objective, decisions, rejections, and source provenance across
  context compaction.
